Record: report on hazard, implemented change and proposed amendment; IRB notification
Party: investigator/institution; investigator; sponsor
Verify: [verify] notifying party not named (passive voice); Investigator chosen because 21 CFR 312.66 places IRB reporting on the investigator; [verify] Whether the 5-working-day window of 21CFR56.104(c) applies to IRB notification of immediate-hazard protocol changes, or only the manner of notification; regulation text gives the cross-reference only (R4-005); [verify] eCFR text of 56.104(c) not retrievable (robots); confirm against eCFR or govinfo before X1 (R4-030)</bpmn:documentation>
